---
import {model,base,assumptions as a,usd,pct,millions} from '../financial-model.mjs';
const y2=base.annual[1];
---
<section id="returns" class="inv-section inv-machine">
<p class="inv-eyebrow">03 / CURRENT MANAGEMENT TARGET · 14 SEPTEMBER 2026</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>Positive projected returns.<br/>Transparent assumptions.</h2><p>The current target models {pct(base.returns.headlineIrr)} five-year headline project IRR for the initial 64-GPU fleet, including assumed terminal recovery and reserve release. It is a conditional projection before investor ownership or a distribution waterfall.</p></div>
<div class="target-pair"><article><span>Target Year 2 · operating project cash</span><strong>{millions(y2.operatingCashUsd)}</strong><p>Gross revenue {millions(y2.revenueUsd)}; EBITDA {millions(y2.ebitdaUsd)}. Operating cash is after modeled operating tax and BC LLC payment, excluding asset sale and reserve release.</p></article><article><span>Target · five-year headline project IRR</span><strong>{pct(base.returns.headlineIrr)}</strong><p>Initial funding {usd(base.capital.totalUsd)}. NPV at the {pct(a.hurdleRate,0)} hurdle is {usd(base.returns.npvUsd)}. The return is positive but below that hurdle; it is not guaranteed.</p></article></div>
<div class="inv-stat-row"><div><strong>$6.50</strong><span>Customer price / B300 GPU-hour</span></div><div><strong>90%</strong><span>Paid utilization target / 21.6 hours daily</span></div><div><strong>20%</strong><span>Marketplace fee on rental revenue</span></div><div><strong>$5.20</strong><span>Per rented hour after fee, before other costs</span></div></div>
<p class="inv-note">60 saleable GPUs × 8,760 hours × 90% paid utilization × $6.50 = {usd(y2.revenueUsd)} annual gross revenue. The fee is {usd(y2.channelFeesUsd)}; all other operating expenses remain included. Paid utilization means rented hours, not hardware uptime. Four installed GPUs are held out of revenue.</p>
<div class="inv-three-col"><article><h3>Launch timing</h3><p>Planned first billing: November 1, 2026. Funding assumed October 1, 2026; one pre-revenue month and eleven operating months in Year 1. Delivery, staffing and commissioning power begin in month 1. This compressed schedule requires execution evidence.</p></article><article><h3>Commercial basis</h3><p>Management reports signed three-year marketplace access. Payment is only for rented hours; no guaranteed occupancy, minimum receipts or protected price. The target assumes $6.50 flat for five years and continued access or replacement channels in Years 4–5.</p></article><article><h3>Cost basis</h3><p>Costs retain the audited v6.1.1 one-building air-cooled budget. The direct-liquid Buildings A/C design requires repricing. Grid energy, demand charges, staffing, internet, insurance, support, tax and site payments remain included.</p></article></div>
<div class="target-table inv-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Current target sensitivity comparison"><table><caption>64 installed / 60 saleable GPUs · recalculated management sensitivities · USD</caption><thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Initial funding</th><th>Year 2 operating cash</th><th>Headline project IRR</th><th>NPV at 15%</th></tr></thead><tbody>{model.scenarios.map(s=><tr><th scope="row">{s.label}</th><td>{usd(s.capital.totalUsd)}</td><td>{usd(s.annual[1].operatingCashUsd)}</td><td>{pct(s.returns.headlineIrr)}</td><td>{usd(s.returns.npvUsd)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p class="inv-note">Slower ramp: 55% paid utilization in the first eleven operating months, then 90%, with flat pricing. Price pressure: 90% utilization and a 10% annual price decline. All cases retain the same cost methods and 20% fee. None clears the 15% hurdle. No return is extrapolated to the 240-GPU target.</p>
{model.scenarios.map(s=><details class="inv-details" open={s.id==='base'}><summary>{s.label} — annual cash flows</summary><div class="target-table inv-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label={s.label+' annual cash flows'}><table><caption>Year 1: October 2026–September 2027 · hold ends September 2031 · USD</caption><thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Operating months</th><th>Gross revenue</th><th>Opex incl. fee</th><th>EBITDA</th><th>Operating cash after tax / site share</th><th>Headline cash incl. exit / reserve</th></tr></thead><tbody>{s.annual.map(y=><tr><th scope="row">{y.year}</th><td>{y.operatingMonths}</td><td>{usd(y.revenueUsd)}</td><td>{usd(y.opexUsd)}</td><td>{usd(y.ebitdaUsd)}</td><td>{usd(y.operatingCashUsd)}</td><td>{usd(y.headlineCashUsd)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="inv-note">Initial funding {usd(s.capital.totalUsd)}; total operating cash {usd(s.returns.totalOperatingCashUsd)}; headline MOIC {s.returns.moic.toFixed(3)}× including exit and reserve. Operating payback: {s.returns.operatingPaybackYears===null?'not reached within five years':s.returns.operatingPaybackYears.toFixed(2)+' modeled years by annual interpolation'}. These are project cash flows, not an investor distribution schedule.</p></details>)}
<p class="inv-note">The target generates {usd(base.returns.totalOperatingCashUsd)} total operating cash, exceeding initial funding by {usd(base.returns.operatingCashSurplusUsd)} before exit. Year-5 asset proceeds {usd(base.annual[4].resaleUsd)}, less {usd(-base.annual[4].resaleTaxUsd)} sale tax, plus {usd(base.annual[4].reserveReleaseUsd)} reserve release contribute to headline IRR. These are not recurring earnings or guaranteed recoveries.</p>
<div class="inv-three-col"><article><h3>Operating assumptions</h3><p>Grid energy {(a.energyUsdPerKwh*100).toFixed(1)}¢/kWh plus {usd(a.demandUsdPerKwMonth)}/billed kW/month. Average PUE {a.averagePue}; inflation {pct(a.annualCostInflation,0)}. Initial internet allowance $4,000/month, subject to carrier scope.</p></article><article><h3>Tax and reserves</h3><p>{pct(a.taxRate,0)} modeled tax; BC LLC receives {pct(a.bcLlcShare,0)} of positive after-tax accounting income. Net-{a.collectionDays} collections; cost reserve plus receivables at inception. Annual modeling does not prove monthly liquidity.</p></article><article><h3>Support and exit</h3><p>{a.includedSupportMonths} operating months of included support, then {pct(a.postWarrantySupportRate,0)} of system cost annually before escalation. Year-5 hardware resale {pct(a.hardwareResaleYear5,0)}, infrastructure recovery {pct(a.infrastructureResale,0)}. Terms remain unverified.</p></article></div>
<div class="inv-actions"><a class="inv-button" href="/api/investor/model" download="SmartTec_Management_Target_2026-09-14.json">Download current model snapshot ↓</a><a class="inv-outline" href="/investors/presentation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open updated investor PDF ↗</a></div>
<details class="inv-details"><summary>Recalculation, provenance and historical comparison</summary><p>The earlier -2.80% Base used different launch, utilization, price-decay and fee assumptions. It is superseded as the headline by this 9.78% target; the original v6.1.1 workbook remains unchanged. Native Excel recalculated temporary Base inputs, followed by independent revenue, fees, expenses, tax, site-payment, cash, IRR and NPV checks.</p><p>Record: {model.source.filename} · reviewed {model.reviewedAt}.</p><p class="target-hash">SHA-256: {model.source.sha256}</p><p>Annual-funded IRR {pct(base.returns.annualFundedIrr)} and dated-funded XIRR {pct(base.returns.datedFundedIrr)} are timing diagnostics. The original workbook is a source cost model; its unmodified Base is not the new target.</p></details>
</section>
<style>
.target-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:2rem;margin:3rem 0}.target-pair article{padding:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,3rem);border:1px solid #aacbb447;border-radius:20px;background:linear-gradient(140deg,#071e17b0,#31624a40)}.target-pair strong{display:block;font-size:clamp(3.5rem,7vw,6.5rem);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:1rem 0;color:#98edac}.target-pair span{font:12px/1.6 var(--f-mono)}.target-table{margin:2rem 0;max-height:none}.target-table table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;min-width:700px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.target-table th,.target-table td{text-align:left;padding:1rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid #a7b9ad55;vertical-align:top}.target-table caption{text-align:left;padding:1rem 0}.target-hash{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.inv-three-col{margin:2rem 0;gap:2rem}@media(max-width:760px){.target-pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}.target-table::before{content:'Swipe horizontally to see all columns →';display:block;position:sticky;left:0;font:11px/1.6 var(--f-mono);padding:.6rem 0;color:#b5e7c4}}
</style>
